    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0141" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Shanghai Round Table/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Japan
                        (Neville)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-27T15:00:00-04:00">May 27, 1932—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. Department’s 119, May 25, 5 p.m., in regard to proposed round table
                    conference. Department desires that you keep in touch also with your French and
                    Italian colleagues. In the course of conversation on May 26 with the French and
                    Italian Ambassadors here, I explained my views on the subject as set forth in
                    the telegram under reference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
